# 2. Remote #

# The same code, with the switch on canister. remoteInstance lives #
# on the Internet Computer, in the backend canister that also holds #
# Hazel's state (docs/internet-computer-backend.md). #

# What happens on an edit: #
#   - the page prints the program, with n already evaluated into it #
#     (the In wire crosses as a Hazel escape, resolved before sending), #
#   - POSTs it to /i/remoteInstance/eval_top on the canister, #
#   - shows "running on the canister..." until the reply arrives, #
#   - and runs again when it does: the reply is the same JSON the #
#     page's own runtime answers, so it becomes the same Hazel value. #

# A reply is kept by its program, so an edit that comes back to an #
# earlier program does not ask again. #

# Pointers are the one difference: what a remote value points at is #
# on the canister, and the read here is synchronous, so a pointer #
# arrives as its name, unread. #

# Opened outside the canister build, this slide says there is no #
# canister to run on. #
let n = 20 in
^^livelit(^fumola_wip((instance = "remoteInstance", name = "", editor = true, bind_input = true, remote = true, tiles = true, input = (n), code = (fumola $graphical as remoteInstance in
  (input * 2, input + 1)
end))))
